``-preview=fastdfa`` detects more escaping references to local variables

With ``-preview=fastdfa``, more cases of returning references to local variables
from ``@safe`` functions are now rejected. For example, returning a slice of a
local static array through another variable is diagnosed
($(LINK2 https://github.com/dlang/dmd/issues/20508, #20508)):

-------
int[] viaVariable() @safe
{
    int[3] a;
    int[] s = a[];
    return s;
} // error: Stack variable exceeds its lifetime by being returned
-------

Behavior without ``-preview=fastdfa`` is unchanged.
